      "judgment_rationale": "The two audited Web project-workspace pages expose list, create and navigation into Blackboard only; settings, membership and Agent-assignment controls belong to the separate Blackboard route tree and are not attributed to these pages. Cloud Desktop wires WorkspaceSettingsDialog through App for update, member add/role update/removal, and Agent bind/unbind calls. Workspace update and Agent binding require editor-or-owner authority, while member add, role update, and removal remain owner-only. Each mutation captures tenant/project/workspace scope epoch and context revision, forwards an AbortSignal to the nested Cloud API, and rejects a result after a scope change before updating the projection. Cloud delete is not exposed. The Local sidecar implements nested list/create only, so Local remains partial."
